  "_comment": [
    "KAN-455. Words in a place name that say what kind of place it is.",
    "One table, two uses in promote_overture_candidates.py:",
    "  1. The venue-word contradiction rule: a chain brand found anywhere in a",
    "     name is refused when another word of the name names a different kind",
    "     of place — `Tasquinha O Salsa` is a tasca, `Cafetaria LIDL Sesimbra` a",
    "     café, `Papelaria Intermarché` a papelaria. `poi_type` contradicts a",
    "     chain of another type; `store_kind` contradicts a chain that is not a",
    "     store or does not carry that kind. Words that fit every store —",
    "     loja, armazém, outlet, galerias, store, shop, house — are not here:",
    "     an absent word is neutral, never a refusal. `parque` and `jardim` are\n     mall and street names (`Decathlon Parque das Nações`, `Benfica Official\n     Store Jardim Regedor`), so `parque` only agrees with the parking category.",
    "  2. `category`: the Overture category the word agrees with, so a chain",
    "     does not overrule it (`IKEA Parking` is the car park). This replaces",
    "     the old CATEGORY_NAME_WORDS.",
    "Keys are matched whole and accent-insensitively (normalize_text), phrases",
    "included. opening_hours.py keys on Foursquare category labels and the",
    "residual join derives its venue words from the data; neither is a word",
    "list and neither overlaps this file."
  ],
